  "independent_assessment": "This correction reads and restricts literal root-directory PAX metadata, rejects ambiguous/global headers and unsafe metadata, preserves the payload extraction no-overwrite policy, and adds a second --overwrite-dir --no-recursion pass selecting only the validated root entry. The updated archive digest is checked by unchanged PVSnapshotDocker resource admission. The helper restores root ownership/mode/time/ACL/xattrs that payload extraction intentionally did not overwrite. It is runtime snapshot restoration behavior, not a supervised graph, criterion, seed, budget, metric, comparison, publisher or Store completion change.",
  "scientific_effect": "No direct criterion-provider input changes and all actual110 triplets remain exact. Restored state and runtime availability still need authentic acquisition/source/executable/journal validation; successful root metadata restoration or compiler/emission exit0 is not evidence of predictive learning, real Metal training or a passing full lane. The source change does not widen the finite-null claim or repair historical floor provenance.",
  "limits": "This assessment reviews delta/evidence scope for the SL criterion decision. It does not approve full cluster down/up, snapshot recovery, live service readiness or production source gates."
